    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE YELLOW TICKET (1914 PLAY)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PLAY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Yellow Ticket (1914 play) is the original work by Michael Morton that inspired the 1931 film and a 1916 film."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICHAEL MORTON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Michael Morton wrote the 1914 play 'The Yellow Ticket', which was later adapted into films."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE YELLOW PASSPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MOVIE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Yellow Passport is an American film based on Michael Morton's 1914 play 'The Yellow Ticket', released in 1916."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1916&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Yellow Passport, an American film based on Michael Morton's 1914 play 'The Yellow Ticket', was released in 1916."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WILLIAM PARKE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"William Parke directed the 1918 film 'The Yellow Ticket', an American silent drama."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FANNIE WARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fannie Ward starred in the 1918 film 'The Yellow Ticket', an American silent drama."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANNA MIRREL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anna Mirrel is the protagonist of the 1918 film 'The Yellow Ticket', a young Jewish girl in Czarist Russia."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CZARIST RUSSIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Czarist Russia is the setting of the 1918 film 'The Yellow Ticket', where Anna Mirrel lives."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ST. PETERSBURG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"St. Petersburg is a city where Anna Mirrel travels to in the 1918 film 'The Yellow Ticket'."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JEWISH GIRL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anna Mirrel is a Jewish girl in Czarist Russia, forced to pretend to be a prostitute to obtain a passport."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PASSPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A passport, referred to as a 'yellow ticket', is an object Anna Mirrel seeks to obtain to visit her father."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FATHER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anna Mirrel's father is a character mentioned in the 1918 film 'The Yellow Ticket', believed to be ill."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YOUNG JOURNALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A young journalist is a character mentioned in the 1918 film 'The Yellow Ticket', who encounters Anna Mirrel."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The state is a concept mentioned in the 1918 film 'The Yellow Ticket', which perpetrates crimes against its citizens."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRIMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crimes are a concept mentioned in the 1918 film 'The Yellow Ticket', committed by the state against its citizens."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTEGRITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Integrity is a concept mentioned in the 1918 film 'The Yellow Ticket', referring to the moral stance of the young journalist."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRE-CODE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pre-Code is a concept mentioned in the 1931 film 'The Yellow Ticket', referring to the era of film production before strict censorship."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SILENT DRAMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENRE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Silent drama is a genre mentioned in the 1918 film 'The Yellow Ticket', describing the type of film it is."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRAMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENRE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Drama is a genre mentioned in the 1931 film 'The Yellow Ticket', describing the type of film it is."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ATTRIBUTE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"American is an attribute mentioned in both films, describing their origin."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FILM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Film is an object mentioned in both films, referring to the medium of the works."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BROADWAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Broadway is a location mentioned in the 1914 play 'The Yellow Ticket', where it was originally produced."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0108-d1a5f809cf6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOHN BARRYMORE&quot;">
